{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1359904-fulfilling-a-character-s-aspiration-get-taken-out","id":1359904,"title":"Fulfilling A Character's Aspiration - Get Taken Out","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-09T09:11:16-08:00","id":1359904,"title":"Fulfilling A Character's Aspiration - Get Taken Out","content":"I have a BK in my game who is pretty optimized for Defense and Soft Armor. I generally need 5-6 successes to overcome his Dodge stunt before even trying to Inflict Injury past his 3+ Soft Armor. He wants to be legitimately Taken Out without any shenanigans. The group I'm planning on doing this with is 3 PKs, each one specialized in one of the PK modes.<br /> <br /> Since the BK doesn't have any dots in Transmogrify, I plan on using one PK to lift him off the ground. That should eliminate his ability to move or use his hand-to-hand attacks. However, he does have 5 dots in Psychomorping. If he activates pretty much all of those powers, I would think Overcome would still grant him enhancements on his Stamina-based Defense roll. Without Transmogrify, I'm wondering if I should exclude him from using the Dodge stunt? Or maybe just limit it since he could still flail his arms and legs around to avoid or block hits but wouldn't be able to do everything he normally does to defend himself?<br /> <br /> Also, does anyone else have some ideas? I realize I can always tell him he can fill his Taken Out box as soon as I do any injury to him, but I think he wants to work through all of his health boxes in order to see what it would take to take his character out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T09:34:47-08:00","id":1359912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1359904-fulfilling-a-character-s-aspiration-get-taken-out#post1359904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a BK in my game who is pretty optimized for Defense and Soft Armor. I generally need 5-6 successes to overcome his Dodge stunt before even trying to Inflict Injury past his 3+ Soft Armor. He wants to be legitimately Taken Out without any shenanigans. The group I'm planning on doing this with is 3 PKs, each one specialized in one of the PK modes.<br /> <br /> Since the BK doesn't have any dots in Transmogrify, I plan on using one PK to lift him off the ground. That should eliminate his ability to move or use his hand-to-hand attacks. However, he does have 5 dots in Psychomorping. If he activates pretty much all of those powers, I would think Overcome would still grant him enhancements on his Stamina-based Defense roll. Without Transmogrify, I'm wondering if I should exclude him from using the Dodge stunt? Or maybe just limit it since he could still flail his arms and legs around to avoid or block hits but wouldn't be able to do everything he normally does to defend himself?<br /> <br /> Also, does anyone else have some ideas? I realize I can always tell him he can fill his Taken Out box as soon as I do any injury to him, but I think he wants to work through all of his health boxes in order to see what it would take to take his character out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shoot him with ship/vehicular Scale weapons. One of the PKs lifts him into the air, another one shoots him with a Hovetank's Heavy Coilgun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T13:06:34-08:00","id":1359950,"title":"","content":"Not a bad idea. It feels a bit like a &quot;rocks fall, every dies&quot; kind of scenario, but I will certainly keep it in my back pocket if nothing else is working.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T15:17:04-08:00","id":1359981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1359904-fulfilling-a-character-s-aspiration-get-taken-out?p=1359950#post1359950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not a bad idea. It feels a bit like a &quot;rocks fall, every dies&quot; kind of scenario, but I will certainly keep it in my back pocket if nothing else is working.</div> </div> </div> </div>If nothing else, it might get him to change his Aspiration to &quot;Don't get Taken Out.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T18:03:12-08:00","id":1360012,"title":"","content":"This seems like a waste of time and an excuse to play,\u201dcan you build a bigger gun than I can build a big tank.\u201d What he\u2019s created doesn\u2019t sound like a legitimate aspiration it sounds like a gauntlet thrown at you. If it were a legitimate aspiration he wouldn\u2019t have thrown the \u201cno shenanigans\u201d nonsense in. He\u2019d just pick a dramatically appropriate time and voluntarily fail and be taken out. Voluntarily failing is entirely meta. It has nothing to do with in-story effort. You\u2019re saying your character tries their best but despite it all it\u2019s not enough because I think it\u2019s more interesting this way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T18:05:00-08:00","id":1360013,"title":"","content":"I seriously think you should tell him that you can play that game if he wants but it\u2019s not going to count as fulfilling an aspiration. \ud83d\udca9","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T18:38:04-08:00","id":1360018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werlynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1359904-fulfilling-a-character-s-aspiration-get-taken-out?p=1360013#post1360013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I seriously think you should tell him that you can play that game if he wants but it\u2019s not going to count as fulfilling an aspiration. \ud83d\udca9</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of agree with that. Figure anything that is capable of legitimately Taking him Out will probably be a Total Party Take Out for everyone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T05:31:35-08:00","id":1360106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werlynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1359904-fulfilling-a-character-s-aspiration-get-taken-out?p=1360012#post1360012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This seems like a waste of time and an excuse to play,\u201dcan you build a bigger gun than I can build a big tank.\u201d What he\u2019s created doesn\u2019t sound like a legitimate aspiration it sounds like a gauntlet thrown at you. If it were a legitimate aspiration he wouldn\u2019t have thrown the \u201cno shenanigans\u201d nonsense in. He\u2019d just pick a dramatically appropriate time and voluntarily fail and be taken out. Voluntarily failing is entirely meta. It has nothing to do with in-story effort. You\u2019re saying your character tries their best but despite it all it\u2019s not enough because I think it\u2019s more interesting this way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I interpreted the &quot;no shenanigans&quot; bit. There's a bit of &quot;I want to see what it would take to seriously threaten my character,&quot; but there is also a story element. His character has been walking around like he's hot shit since he's come through all the combats with basically no injuries. So, he wants to see his character humbled and play through a shake-up to his self-esteem. That's why I think he wants it with no shenanigans. He wants to the loss to feel earned. He's just set the bar high, mechanically. However, you are correct, the loss could be narratively earned without necessarily being mechanically difficult. I might try to push him in that direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T05:45:50-08:00","id":1360108,"title":"","content":"You can take him down with non physical attacks, Telepathy for example, or he can be teleported to the space with no suit, or using quantakinesis to disable his BK.<br /> <br /> Or even worse, the enemy start controlling him to use as his own tank.<br /> <br /> If the idea is to show him where it hurts go against his weak points not against his armor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T11:36:21-08:00","id":1360175,"title":"","content":"A Terat could probably do the trick.<br /> <br /> That said, if you are looking to humble them, it could also be a situation where they aren't necessarily incapacitated, but are occupied and unable to save someone <i>else.</i> For all their power they can't protect their loved ones kinda thing. I only recommend this if it is a story beat they are looking for, because it could be a bit of a dick move otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T19:27:32-08:00","id":1360268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1359904-fulfilling-a-character-s-aspiration-get-taken-out?p=1360108#post1360108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can take him down with non physical attacks, Telepathy for example, or he can be teleported to the space with no suit, or using quantakinesis to disable his BK.<br /> <br /> Or even worse, the enemy start controlling him to use as his own tank.<br /> <br /> If the idea is to show him where it hurts go against his weak points not against his armor.</div> </div> </div> </div>hull breach. Not much adaptation might keep them alive but not much it can do to arrest their velocity away from the ship off into the cold dark of space. Then adaptation\u2019s survival ability might be a liability<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}